# QM/MM surface hopping driven by the ANALYTIC MRSF NAC (scheme=NAC), the
# route this branch enables for embedded dynamics: tdc=analytic evaluates the
# S0/S1 derivative coupling analytically at every overlap interval inside the
# ESPF field, and rescale=analytic_nac contracts the velocity along it.
#
# Formaldehyde (QM, atoms 0-3) in 5 TIP3P waters (MM), non-periodic.  The QM
# region is a whole molecule, so the partition cuts no bond and there are no
# link atoms -- analytic NAC is refused with a link atom, because a
# link-centre coupling direction cannot be projected onto real atoms.
#
# The analytic route has an accuracy guard: it needs a two-SOMO ROHF/ROKS
# triplet reference, singlet MRSF states, and scf/tdhf conv <= 1e-8, hence the
# tightened thresholds below.  nstep=2 reaches the second overlap interval,
# which is where the coupling is first evaluated.  velocity=zero keeps the two
# steps reproducible.  Requires the optional OpenMM backend.
mrsf(nstate=2)/bhhlyp/6-31g* namd(S1,scheme=NAC)
md(nstep=2,dt=0.5,velocity=zero,seed=3,trajectory_interval=1,trajectory_file="H2CO-water-nac.namd.trj")
qmmm(pdb_file="formaldehyde_water.pdb",forcefield_files="formaldehyde.xml tip3p.xml",qm_atoms="0-3",cutoff=NoCutoff)
scf(conv=1e-9,maxit=200)
tdhf(conv=1e-9,maxit=100)
geom="../geometries/CH2O-2bc62dda4b8a.xyz"
